---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Diagram from '../components/Diagram.astro';

const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is dkim in simple terms?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Do I need to memorize all of this?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How long does it take to implement?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What happens if I get it wrong?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Is this the same across all DNS providers?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Where can I get help if I'm stuck?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout title="DKIM Explained: DomainKeys Identified Mail" description="DKIM explained: how cryptographic signatures prove your email wasn't forged, how selectors and keys work, and how to set DKIM up."  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">DKIM</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">DKIM Explained</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      SPF lists <em>who may send</em>. DKIM proves <em>the mail itself is intact</em>: every message
      is cryptographically signed with a private key, and receivers verify the signature against the
      public key you publish in DNS.
    </p>
    <Diagram name="dkim-signing" caption="How DKIM signing and verification work" />


    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2>How it works, end to end</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your sending server generates a key pair. The <strong>private key</strong> stays on the server; the <strong>public key</strong> goes into DNS at <code>selector._domainkey.yourdomain.com</code>.</li>
        <li>Each outgoing message gets a <code>DKIM-Signature</code> header covering the important headers and body, tagged with the selector used.</li>
        <li>The receiver's mail server fetches that public key from DNS and verifies the signature. Valid = the mail genuinely came from your domain and wasn't modified in transit.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Selectors: one domain, many keys</h2>
      <p>
        The selector is the label in the DNS name (<code>google._domainkey…</code>,
        <code>k1._domainkey…</code>, <code>s1._domainkey…</code>). It lets every service you send
        through publish its own key without collisions, which is also why you must tell any checker
        <em>which</em> selector to look up. Use the <a href="/dkim-record-checker/">DKIM checker</a>
        with the selector your provider documents.
      </p>

      <h2>Key strength matters</h2>
      <p>
        1024-bit RSA keys are considered weak today; some receivers refuse them outright. 2048-bit is
        the standard recommendation (ed25519 is the modern alternative). Rotating keys is normal,
        publish the new selector before retiring the old one so in-flight mail still verifies.
      </p>

      <h2>DKIM + the rest</h2>
      <p>
        DKIM passes are one of the two inputs <a href="/dmarc/">DMARC</a> evaluates (SPF is the other).
        Gmail and Yahoo's sender requirements make both effectively mandatory for bulk mail. Check
        your whole stack at once, SPF, DKIM, DMARC, DNSSEC, in the
        <a href="/">homepage security scanner</a>.
      </p>

      
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is dkim in simple terms?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Do I need to memorize all of this?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does it take to implement?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What happens if I get